  "rationale": "The workflow is a minimal manual release job that only calls the pre-installed `gh` CLI. It has no dependency installation, test steps, matrix jobs, or scheduled triggers. The existing `concurrency: group: release` already cancels superseded runs (implementing P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE). No evidence-supported optimization applies: caching (P-LIT-GHA-CACHE) has no dependencies to cache; timeout (P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT) lacks evidence of runaway jobs in 5 successful historical runs (9-14s each); other patterns require matrix, schedules, tests, or build steps not present. Adding a timeout would be speculative and unrelated to observed behavior.",
